mount_text.subtree_refusal:
mode 'subtree' needs one command `init` must not run for you — `git subtree add` creates commits, and commits are the owner's (D5). Run it, then re-run init:
    git subtree add --prefix {{relative}} {{repo}} {{pin}} --squash
    {{cli}} init --mode subtree --ref {{pin}}

mount_text.switch_old_mount:
switching mount mode {{previous}} → {{mode}} needs the old mount gone first — `init` does not delete a tree it did not create, and the removal is your commit (D5). Retire {{relative}}, then re-run:
{{removal}}
    {{cli}} init --mode {{target}} --switch-mode

